messages:    4%|3         | 22/600 [00:11<04:55,  1.96it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA street comprehensive management committee has a total of 6 members: F, G, H, I, M and P. Each of these members shall serve as a member of at least one of the three sub-committees under the Comprehensive Management Committee. Each sub-committee consists of three different members. The known information is as follows: one of the six members serves as a member of three subcommittees. F is not a member of the same subcommittee as G. H is not a member of the same subcommittee as I.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options must be true?\n# Options:\nA) One of f or g is a member of three sub-committees.\nB) One of h or i is a member of three sub-committees.\nC) P or m is a member of only one sub-committee.\nD) One member happens to be a member of the two sub-committees.', "To solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the information and analyze each option step by step.\n\n### Given Information:\n1.There are 6 members: F, G, H, I, M, and P.\n2.Each member serves in at least one of the three sub-committees.\n3.Each sub-committee consists of three different members.\n4.No member serves in any of the three sub-committees.\n5.F is in the same subcommittee as G.\n6.H is in the same subcommittee as I.\n\n### Analysis of Options:\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
