messages:   16%|#5        | 94/600 [01:07<12:07,  1.44s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe words we follow today to talk about ancient Chinese painting are all written by Chinese literati, and because of this, Chinese literati have dominated the discussion space of painting for a long time, and they have become accustomed to starting from their own point of view. choose a point of view that is good for literati and artists, and now-- or should have been-- it's time for us to compete with them. And we should also question what they call a good painter or good work. Many excellent non-literati artists do not get due recognition because of the prejudice of literati. Here, we should give them objective evaluation and due status one by one.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements is consistent with the original text?\n# Options:\nA) The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice\nC) The literati have been in a strong position in the field of chinese painting theory for a long time\nD) The difference of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting has a long history", 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option in relation to the provided information.\n\nThe context discusses the dominance of Chinese literati in the discussion and evaluation of ancient Chinese painting.It mentions that literati have been accustomed to viewing and evaluating paintings from their own perspective, which has led to a bias against non-literati artists.The text suggests that it\'s time to challenge this perspective and give non-literati artists the recognition they deserve.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) "The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level.".\n- The context does not provide any information about the appreciation level of literati artists compared to their creative level.This statement is not supported by the text.\n\nB) "In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice.".\n- The text mentions that non-literati artists do not get due recognition because of the prejudice of literati, but it does not specifically state that talented literati and artists were buried due to prejudice.This statement is not consistent with the text.\n\nThe difference of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting has not been historically significant.\n- The text does not provide evidence of any substantial differences in interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting. This option contradicts the text.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
