messages:   25%|##4       | 148/600 [01:49<04:01,  1.87it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe literary works of the Chinese writer Mo Yan have made the hidden Chinese vernacular concerned by the readers of the world and recognized by the international literary world, which has once again proved that this judgment is that only the national is the world.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, based on this, which of the following options is correct?\n# Options:\nA) It's national, it's world\nB) If it is not national, it is not world\nC) As long as the nation is, it is the world\nD) Only the world is national", 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option in relation to the given statement.\n\nThe context states that Mo Yan\'s works have brought attention to Chinese vernacular and have been recognized internationally.This recognition is used to support the idea that "only the national is the world.".\n\nLet\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) It\'s national, it\'s world.\n- This option suggests that if something is national, it is automatically world-renowned.This is close to the idea presented in the context but not exactly the same.The context implies that being national is a prerequisite for being recognized globally, but it does not state that all national things are world-renowned.\n\nB) If it is not national, it is not world.\n- This option suggests that something must be national to be recognized globally.This aligns well with the context, which states that only the national is the world.If something is not national, it cannot be considered world-renowned according to the given statement.Only something national is recognized globally.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
