messages:   29%|##9       | 175/600 [02:00<05:04,  1.40it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nDirectional movement refers to the directional motion caused by the external stimulation of plants in a single direction, including positive motion, gravity movement, tactile motion and directional motion. Most of the directional movement is growth movement, which is an irreversible process of motion.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is a directional movement, as defined above?\n# Options:\nA) The puppy, lured repeatedly by the bone, sees the bone again and continues to droouff\nB) The roots of rice always grow in the direction of more fertilizer in the soil\nC) The petals of the cow spread in the morning, and when the sun shines directly at noon, the petals close\nD) Plants that prefer shade grow better in the shade than in direct sunlight', "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option describes a directional movement as defined in the context.The context specifies that directional movement is caused by external stimulation in a single direction and is mostly a growth movement that is irreversible.\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) The puppy, lured repeatedly by the bone, sees the bone again and continues to drool.\n- This option describes a behavioral response in an animal, not a plant.It also does not involve growth movement or external stimulation causing directional motion.Therefore, it does not fit the definition of directional movement.\n\nB) The roots of rice always grow in the direction of more fertilizer in the soil.\n- This option describes the roots of rice growing towards a source of fertilizer, which is an external stimulation causing directional growth.This fits the definition of directional movement as it involves growth movement in response to external stimulation.\nPlants that thrive in sunlight grow better when exposed to direct sunlight than when placed in the shade.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
