messages:   30%|###       | 180/600 [02:08<10:01,  1.43s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIt is generally believed that honesty is a matter of personal morality and has nothing to do with others, but personal morality is not only a personal problem, but it will also produce social effects through externalities-the debt that individuals get, Eventually, it may repay to the whole society. From the perspective of institutional economics, a good economic system and governance mechanism should be able to restrain negative externalities, otherwise the economic order may collapse. It is necessary to make the initiators bear their due responsibility through the system and mechanism, rather than letting others or the whole market pay for it.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the most accurate summary of the main point of this passage?\n# Options:\nA) It is true that personal morality has to be paid for by the whole society\nB) The economic system is of great significance to the economic order\nC) Honesty is both a social issue and an economic issue\nD) System is needed to suppress negative externalities of dishonesty', 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option in relation to the main point of the passage.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - The passage starts by discussing the belief that honesty is a personal matter.\n   - It then argues that personal morality (like honesty) has social effects through externalities.\n   - It mentions that a good economic system and governance mechanism should restrain negative externalities.\n   - The passage concludes by emphasizing the need for a system to ensure that those who initiate negative externalities bear their own responsibility, rather than others or the market paying for it.\n\n2.**Option Analysis:**.\n   - **Option A:** "It is true that personal morality has to be paid for by the whole society.".\n     - This option is partially correct but not the main point.The passage does mention that personal morality can have social effects, but it doesn\'t state that personal morality always has to be paid for by society.\n   - **Option B:** "The economic system is of great significance to the economic order.".\n     - This option is true but too broad.The passage focuses more on the role of the system in managing externalities rather than just the significance of the economic system.The need for a system to manage and suppress negative externalities caused by dishonesty is not important.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
