messages:   36%|###6      | 216/600 [02:28<07:54,  1.24s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nTechnological innovation refers to the first application of a new technology or invention in production and the establishment of a new production or supply function in the production system in the theory of economic development, introduce a new combination of production factors and production conditions. Economics emphasizes that technological innovation has the characteristics of non-exclusiveness, uncertainty, marketability and systemicity.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following behaviors belongs to technological innovation in the field of economics?\n# Options:\nA) In europe, the concorde flew successfully. airfares are extremely expensive because of the high cost of flying.\nB) The space technology of the united states is extremely advanced and the space shuttle flies freely in space.\nC) After a long period of formula testing, wuliangye launched a low alcohol wine on the market and achieved excellent market returns.\nD) Iridium's technology allows people to send and receive messages from anywhere on earth.", 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option best fits the definition of technological innovation provided in the context.The definition emphasizes the following characteristics:.\n1.First application of a new technology or invention in production.\n2.Establishment of a new production or supply function.\n3.Introduction of a new combination of production factors and production conditions.\n4.Non-exclusiveness, uncertainty, marketability, and systemicity.\n\nLet\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) "In Europe, the Concorde flew successfully.Airfares are extremely expensive because of the high cost of flying.".\n- This option describes a successful flight but does not mention a new production function or marketability.It focuses on the high cost of airfares, which does not align with the characteristics of technological innovation.\n\nB) "The space technology of the United States is extremely advanced and the space shuttle flies freely in space.".\n- This option highlights advanced space technology but does not specify a new production function or marketability.It neglects the potential of the space shuttle, which perfectly aligns with the definition.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
