messages:   38%|###7      | 226/600 [02:32<02:06,  2.96it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnalogical argument is based on the sameness or similarity of two objects in some attributes, and infers that the two objects are also the same or similar in other attributes. Its logical form is that object A has the attributes of a, b, c and d. Object B has properties of a, b, c. So object B has the property of d.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the followings belongs to analogical argument?\n# Options:\nA) Tao yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, li bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. this shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries\nB) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation\nC) Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, comrade bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that comrade bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others\nD) Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper', "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option fits the definition of an analogical argument provided in the context.The definition states that an analogical argument is based on the sameness or similarity of two objects in some attributes and infers that the two objects are also the same or similar in other attributes.The logical form is that if object A has attributes a, b, c, and d, and object B has attributes a, b, and c, then object B is inferred to have attribute d.\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) This option compares Tao Yuanming and Li Bai, stating that both do not bow to power or wealth, and concludes that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries.This is more of a generalization about ambitious people rather than an analogical argument based on the similarity of two specific objects.\n\nB) This option compares light and sound, noting that both have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction, and reflection, and infers that light, like sound, also has fluctuation.This fits the definition of an analogical argument because it uses the similarity in some attributes (linear propagation, refraction, reflection) to infer a similarity in another attribute (fluctuation).\nBased on the analysis, the option that fits the definition of an analogical argument is not D, but rather C.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
