messages:   41%|####      | 245/600 [02:53<02:59,  1.98it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNew research shows that improving the reflectivity of urban roofs and road surfaces may reduce the temperature of the earth's atmosphere at a very low cost. Although the reduction is small, it can be measured. Because roofs and roads account for more than 60% of the city's surface area, the use of light-colored materials can increase the average reflectivity to a certain extent, reducing the global average temperature by as much as 0.07 degrees Celsius, according to researchers in the Environmental Research report.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to this passage, which of the following is understood correctly?\n# Options:\nA) The new material can greatly reduce the indoor temperature\nB) Urban road surface accounts for more than half of the total urban area\nC) People are exploring new ways to alleviate global warming\nD) The surface of dark materials has strong reflectivity", 'Let\'s analyze each option based on the context provided:.\n\nA) The new material can greatly reduce the indoor temperature.\n- The passage does not mention anything about the indoor temperature.It focuses on the reflectivity of urban roofs and road surfaces and their effect on the global average temperature.Therefore, this option is not supported by the passage.\n\nB) Urban road surface accounts for more than half of the total urban area.\n- The passage states that "roofs and roads account for more than 60% of the city\'s surface area."This means that roads alone do not necessarily account for more than half of the total urban area, but together with roofs, they do.Therefore, this option is not precisely correct based on the information given.\n\nC) People are exploring new ways to alleviate global warming.\nThe surface of dark materials lacks strong reflectivity. Therefore, this option is correct.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
