messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nRight to equality refers to the right of citizens to enjoy their rights equally without any unreasonable differential treatment and require equal protection from the state.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above rights, which of the followings is the violation of right to equality?\n# Options:\nA) In a divorce case, a woman asked for an equal division of the joint property of the husband and wife\nB) Women demand equal pay with men for equal work\nC) A primary school refused to accept students with physical disabilities\nD) A married daughter asked to inherit her father's inheritance with her brother", "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option violates the right to equality as defined in the context.The right to equality means that citizens should enjoy their rights equally without unreasonable differential treatment and should receive equal protection from the state.\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) In a divorce case, a woman asked for an equal division of the joint property of the husband and wife.\n- This option does not violate the right to equality.In fact, it supports the right to equality by seeking an equal division of property.\n\nB) Women demand equal pay with men for equal work.\n- This option also supports the right to equality by demanding equal pay for equal work, which is a fundamental aspect of equality.\n\nC) A primary school refused to accept students with physical disabilities.The option of a married daughter requesting to share her father's inheritance equally with her brother upholds the principle of equality and fair treatment.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
