messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe term boundary problem refers to various short-sighted behaviors of employees due to the short employment relationship in modern enterprises, and the harm caused by such behaviors to the enterprise\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings belongs to the term boundary problem\n# Options:\nA) Because he will retire in one year, lao zhao feels unable and his work efficiency is getting worse and worse\nB) Because he was not familiar with the business, xiao li, who had just come a month, lost a big customer and the company lost a lot\nC) Because he felt that it was impossible to become a regular worker,xiao wang worked hard every day to show himself \nD) Because he only signed a contract for half a year, xiao sun ignored the use of working machinery and equipment', 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option best fits the definition of a "boundary problem."The context defines a boundary problem as short-sighted behaviors of employees due to short-term employment relationships and the harm caused by such behaviors to the enterprise.\n\nLet\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) Lao Zhao feels unable and his work efficiency is getting worse and worse because he will retire in one year.\n- This option describes a decline in work efficiency due to impending retirement, which is not directly related to a short-term employment relationship.It does not fit the definition of a boundary problem.\n\nB) Xiao Li, who had just come a month, lost a big customer and the company lost a lot because he was not familiar with the business.\n- This option describes a mistake due to lack of familiarity with the business, but it does not indicate short-sighted behavior due to a short-term employment relationship.It does not fit the definition of a boundary problem.\n\nD) Xiao Sun diligently utilized the working machinery and equipment, despite having a long-term contract in place.\n- This scenario illustrates an employee conscientiously using equipment even with a lengthy contract, which is opposite to negligent behavior.It does not suggest short-sightedness or harm to the enterprise.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
