messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOur parents pay more and more attention to children's reading. Most parents want their children to read more and read better books. In 2018,70.3 percent of families in one city had the habit of parents reading with their children. The amount of books read by parents and children increased by 1.8 percentage points compared to 2017 and the length of books read also increased compared to last year. But in 2018, the city's children read just 4.72 books per person, down 0.6 percentage points from 2017.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, best explains the phenomenon?\n# Options:\nA) In recent years, children have a heavy burden of schoolwork and many people want to read extracurricular reading but do not have enough time.\nB) Most parents born in the 1980s and 1990s are highly educated and value reading for their children.\nC) Many children are used to listening to books in parent-child reading, which is not counted in 2018.\nD) Electronic reading by parents on mobile phones and computers has not been taken into account in children's books.", "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify the phenomenon that needs explaining and then analyze each option to see which one best accounts for the given data.\n\nThe phenomenon to explain is:.\n- Despite an increase in the habit of parents reading with their children and an increase in the amount and length of books read, the number of books read per person by children decreased.\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) **In recent years, children have a heavy burden of schoolwork and many people want to read extracurricular reading but do not have enough time.**.\n   - This option suggests that children are busy with schoolwork and thus have less time for reading.However, it does not directly explain why the number of books read per person decreased despite an increase in reading habits and the amount of books read.\n\nB) **Most parents born in the 1980s and 1990s are highly educated and value reading for their children.**.\n   - This option explains why parents might be more involved in reading with their children, but it does not explain the decrease in the number of books read per person by children.\n\nC) **Many children are used to listening to books in parent-child reading, which is not counted in 2018.This option implies that electronic reading by parents on mobile phones and computers has been considered in children's books, which directly addresses the decrease in the number of books read per person by children. Despite an increase in reading habits and the amount of books read, Option C does not provide a plausible reason for the phenomenon.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
