messages:   62%|######1   | 370/600 [04:02<01:13,  3.11it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, as tourism exploration has become more and more popular by some people, there are more and more rescue operations. Should we charge for the deployment of public resources to rescue tourism explorers who commit intentional adventures? These issues have also become the topic that everyone is most concerned about. The positive side thinks that it should be charged; the opposite side thinks that it should not be charged.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, cannot support the positive side's point of view?\n# Options:\nA) A rational citizen should be responsible for his own actions; otherwise, it will be unfair to other taxpayers\nB) The establishment of a professional rescue system requires a certain amount of financial support\nC) It is the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress. simple charges can not help adventurers build up a sense of social responsibility\nD) Tourist explorers who illegally enter unsafe areas and waste social resources and taxpayers' money should bear the corresponding expenses", 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option does not support the positive side\'s point of view, which argues that rescue operations for intentional adventurers should be charged.\n\nLet\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) "A rational citizen should be responsible for his own actions; otherwise, it will be unfair to other taxpayers.".\n- This supports the positive side\'s point of view because it emphasizes personal responsibility and fairness to taxpayers.\n\nB) "The establishment of a professional rescue system requires a certain amount of financial support.".\n- This supports the positive side\'s point view because it implies that financial support (which could come from charging for rescue operations) is necessary for the rescue system.\n\nC) "It is the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress.Simple charges cannot help adventurers build up a sense of social responsibility.".\n- This does not support the positive side\'s point of view.It supports the positive side\'s point of view, proposing that charging for rescues can effectively build social responsibility.\n\nA) "Law-abiding adventurers who responsibly navigate safe areas and contribute to social resources and taxpayers\' money should not bear the corresponding expenses.".\n- This contradicts the negative side\'s argument by suggesting that those who utilize resources appropriately should not be responsible for the cost of rescue operations.\n\nConsidering the examination, the option that cannot support the positive side\'s point of view is:.\n\nB) "Private companies should handle all rescue operations, as this ensures a more efficient use of resources and encourages personal accountability.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
