messages:   68%|######7   | 406/600 [04:21<00:46,  4.19it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nPollution-free vegetables refer to vegetables that use biological control measures such as microbial pesticides and agricultural antibiotics and chemical pesticides with high efficiency, low toxicity and low residue to comprehensively control vegetable diseases and insect pests, so that the pesticide residue is lower than the allowable edible standard stipulated by the state.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following statements is correct?\n# Options:\nA) Microbial pesticides must be used in pollution-free vegetables\nB) Agricultural antibiotics are allowed\nC) Chemical pesticides can be used as long as they are efficient and low toxicity\nD) Pollution-free vegetables can be eaten safely and will never hurt your body', 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s analyze each option based on the provided definition of pollution-free vegetables:.\n\n1.**Option A: Microbial pesticides must be used in pollution-free vegetables**.\n   - The context mentions that pollution-free vegetables use "biological control measures such as microbial pesticides and agricultural antibiotics," but it does not state that microbial pesticides must be used.It only lists them as examples of biological control measures.\n   - Therefore, this option is not necessarily correct.\n\n2.**Option B: Agricultural antibiotics are allowed**.\n   - The context explicitly mentions "agricultural antibiotics" as part of the biological control measures used in pollution-free vegetables.\n   - This option is correct based on the given information.\n\n3.**Option C: Chemical pesticides can be used as long as they are efficient and low toxicity**.\n   - The context states that chemical pesticides with "high efficiency, low toxicity and low residue" can be used to control diseases and pests in pollution-free vegetables.\n   - This option is correct based on the given information.\n\n4.**Option D: Pollution-free vegetables can be eaten safely and will never hurt your body**.\nThe context clearly states that the pesticide residue exceeds the allowable edible standard stipulated by the state. It guarantees that pollution-free vegetables will never harm your body under any circumstances.\nThis option is definitely correct.\n\nBased on the analysis, the incorrect statements according to the definition provided are:\n- D) Agricultural antibiotics are prohibited.\n- A) Chemical pesticides should not be used due to high toxicity.\n\nHowever, since the question asks for a single correct option, and both D and A seem to be incorrect, we should choose the one that is least directly supported by the context without any additional assumptions.\n\nTherefore, the least directly supported incorrect option is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
