messages:   71%|#######   | 424/600 [04:29<01:36,  1.83it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn Berinia, the age at which people could begin to drink alcohol legally used to be 18. In 1990, in an attempt to reduce alcohol consumption and thereby to reduce alcohol-related traffic deaths among Berinians under 21, the legal drinking age was raised to 21. Alcohol-related traffic deaths among people under 21 have decreased significantly since 1990. Nevertheless, surveys show that people in that age-group drink just as much alcohol as they did before 1990.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true of Berinia, most helps to resolve the apparent discrepancy?\n# Options:\nA) Alcohol-related traffic deaths among people over 21 have increased slightly since 1990.\nB) For the population as a whole, annual alcohol consumption is no lower now than it was in 1990.\nC) The proportion of people under 21 who own a car is higher now than it was in 1990.\nD) Alcohol consumption away from home, for example in bars and restaurants, is much lower among people under 21 than it was in 1990.', "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify the apparent discrepancy and find the option that best resolves it.The context presents a situation where the legal drinking age was raised to 21 in an attempt to reduce alcohol-related traffic deaths among those under 21.Despite surveys showing that people under 21 still drink as much as before, alcohol-related traffic deaths among this age group have decreased significantly.\n\nThe apparent discrepancy is that even though young people are drinking the same amount of alcohol, the number of alcohol-related traffic deaths has decreased.\n\nLet's analyze each option to see which one helps resolve this discrepancy:.\n\nA) Alcohol-related traffic deaths among people over 21 have increased slightly since 1990.\n- This option does not address the behavior or traffic deaths of the under-21 group.It talks about a different age group, so it does not help resolve the discrepancy.\n\nB) For the population as a whole, annual alcohol consumption is no lower now than it was in 1990.\n- This option provides information about the overall population's alcohol consumption but does not explain why alcohol-related traffic deaths among the under-21 group have decreased.\n\nC) The proportion of people under 21 who own a car is higher now than it was in 1990.Option D does not provide a plausible explanation for the decrease in alcohol-related traffic deaths among people under 21, despite their overall alcohol consumption remaining the same.Therefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
