messages:   73%|#######3  | 439/600 [04:35<00:36,  4.43it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nFor example, X X Group held an anniversary celebration, your mobile phone number won a grand prize of 100000 yuan. this kind of unwise fraudulent text messages on mobile phones still appear again and again even after they have been exposed by the media. Professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy fraudulent text messages rather than design more deceptive and gullible text messages, which only shows that the swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options, if true, strongly refutes the above conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\nD) Swindlers use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they want to filter out smart people in the first place.', "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify the conclusion and then find which option, if true, would strongly refute it.The conclusion in the context is that the swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional because they continue to use shoddy fraudulent text messages.\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\n- This option suggests that swindlers need to be smart to deceive, but it does not directly address why they continue to use shoddy messages.It does not refute the conclusion that they are unprofessional.\n\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\n- This option talks about avoiding police attention, which is not directly related to the quality of the fraudulent text messages or the professionalism of the swindlers.It does not refute the conclusion.Swindlers employ text messages to entice individuals who are easily fooled, and they aim to attract intelligent individuals initially.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
