messages:   78%|#######8  | 470/600 [04:40<00:18,  6.90it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe scene of the times has changed so much that in order for the younger generation to really remember history, we should not stop at conceptual preaching. A truly complete and effective history education should be integrated into life. It should not only be seen in memorials and in books, It should also infiltrate into the neighborhoods and scenes of our lives in a rich and appropriate form. Only in this way can it be transformed into the collective memory of the whole nation.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is an accurate summary of this passage?\n# Options:\nA) The significance of history education\nB) The form of history education should be lifelike\nC) History education is available anytime, anywhere\nD) History exists in the collective memory of the nation', "To solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the context and analyze each option in relation to the passage.\n\nThe passage emphasizes the need for history education to be more than just conceptual preaching.It suggests that for the younger generation to truly remember history, the education should be integrated into daily life, not just confined to memorials and books.The goal is to make history education so pervasive that it becomes part of the collective memory of the nation.\n\nNow, let's analyze each option:.\n\nA) The significance of history education.\n- This option is too broad.While the passage does touch on the importance of history education, it focuses more on how it should be delivered rather than just its significance.\n\nB) The form of history education should be lifelike.\nHistory education should only be available in specific locations at certain times, making it less accessible to the public and harder to relate to.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
