messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, monosodium glutamate, a family essential product, has been questioned by people. It has been proposed that adding monosodium glutamate in the cooking process has a great harmful effect on the human body. Eating too much monosodium glutamate will lead to hair loss, vision loss, zinc deficiency, and even cancer or other visceral diseases. However, according to research, monosodium glutamate can enhance people's appetite, Improve the human body's ability to absorb other things and have a certain tonic effect on the human body.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is correct according to the above materials?\n# Options:\nA) Adding monosodium glutamate during cooking may have a great harmful effect on human body\nB) Msg may cause cancer or other visceral diseases\nC) Monosodium glutamate can improve people's food and martial arts, and has a certain tonic effect on the human body\nD) Monosodium glutamate is safe and safe to eat", 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s analyze each option based on the provided context:.\n\nA) "Adding monosodium glutamate during cooking may have a great harmful effect on human body.".\n- The context mentions that it has been proposed that adding monosodium glutamate can have harmful effects, including hair loss, vision loss, zinc deficiency, and even cancer or other visceral diseases.However, it also states that research shows monosodium glutamate can have beneficial effects.This option is partially correct but does not capture the full picture provided by the context.\n\nB) "Msg may not cause cancer or other visceral diseases.".\n- The context does not mention that eating too much monosodium glutamate can lead to cancer or other visceral diseases.This statement is directly contradicted by the context.\n\nC) "Monosodium glutamate can worsen people\'s food and martial arts, and has no tonic effect on the human body."\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
