messages:   87%|########7 | 523/600 [04:57<00:34,  2.20it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nRecently, a number of emotional intelligence education institutions have launched corresponding packages for different age groups. Emotional intelligence classes are popular among parents. Emotional intelligence is the ability to control and manage emotions, and it plays an important role in people's life and work. However, in the hearts of many people, the connotation of emotional intelligence has been alienated. The earliest concept of emotional intelligence is very different from the popular concept of emotional intelligence today. Many people's understanding of emotional intelligence is another way of saying sophistication and flattery. In fact, the core of emotional intelligence is not only the ability to recognize and control one's own emotions, but also the ability to communicate with others and integrate into the collective. The cultivation of these two abilities needs to be practiced in daily life. Whether children can develop good emotional control and social skills depends to a large extent on their parents, and no EQ training can replace the EQ training in daily life.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is most likely to be described next?\n# Options:\nA) Emotional intelligence tutoring should arouse great attention from parents\nB) Parents' practice in family education\nC) Parents should view emotional intelligence training courses rationally\nD) Need to cultivate and improve parents' emotional intelligence", "To solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the context and analyze each option in relation to the information provided.\n\nThe context discusses the popularity of emotional intelligence (EQ) education among parents and the misconceptions surrounding EQ.It emphasizes that EQ is not just about recognizing and controlling one's emotions but also about communication and integration into a collective.The passage also highlights that the development of these skills largely depends on parents and cannot be replaced by EQ training courses alone.\n\nNow, let's analyze each option:.\n\nA) Emotional intelligence tutoring should arouse great attention from parents.\n- This option suggests that parents should pay more attention to EQ tutoring.However, the passage already mentions that EQ classes are popular among parents, so this option doesn't seem to be the next logical step.\n\nB) Parents' practice in family education.\n- This option aligns well with the passage's emphasis on the role of parents in developing EQ in children.The passage states that EQ training cannot replace the EQ training in daily life, which implies the importance of parents' practice in family education.Parents should not bother improving their emotional intelligence.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
