messages:   96%|#########5| 573/600 [05:29<00:10,  2.56it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSelf depletion phenomenon is a phenomenon in which individuals' ability or willingness to conduct voluntary activities decline in the process of long-term work, including the decline in ability or willingness to control the environment, control themselves, make choices and initiate behaviors, and at the same time, job burnout, self depletion but no progress.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is self depletion phenomenon?\n# Options:\nA) Lee did not finish his doctoral thesis and continued to postpone it. as a result, he did not graduate from school for eight years\nB) Chen has worked as a deputy director of the magazine for 20 years, and although he has published some personal works, he has not been promoted\nC) Song mou do sales work for nearly ten years, although he changed four or five companies, but because the performance is average, the income has not changed\nD) Wang has been working as an archive administrator for 15 years. he feels numb to his work and has no desire to change the status quo and get promoted", "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option best fits the definition of the self depletion phenomenon provided in the context.The key elements of self depletion are:.\n1.Decline in ability or willingness to conduct voluntary activities.\n2.Decline in ability or willingness to control the environment, control oneself, make choices, and initiate behaviors.\n3.Job burnout.\n4.Self depletion but no progress.\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) Lee did not finish his doctoral thesis and continued to postpone it.As a result, he did not graduate from school for eight years.\n- This scenario shows a lack of progress and a decline in the ability to complete tasks, but it does not explicitly mention job burnout or a long-term work context.\n\nThis scenario clearly demonstrates a strong work ethic, enthusiasm for career growth, and a desire to take on new challenges and advance in the workplace.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
